I go into the kitchen.
There is a small gas stove there.
I make coffee on that stove.
This is coffee from my home country.
Two mugs sit on top of the counter.
I pour hot coffee into the mugs.
Anitha is in the living room now.
She sits on the sofa.
I give a mug of coffee to Anitha.
I sit next to her.
"Maya, this coffee is very good," Anitha says.
"This is coffee from Mexico," I say.
We drink the coffee together.
There is a lot of peace in the flat.
The new plant sits near the window.
I am very happy now.
